 "notes": [
  {
   "recipe": "Cherry Phosphate Shortbread Thumbprints",
   "notes": "Built on your proven Jam Thumbprint proportions (egg yolk only, no added liquid, no baking soda) so the wells hold. Cream butter, sugar and honey; beat in yolk and extracts; mix in flour, cherry powder, baking powder and salt. Roll 1 in. balls, press wells, chill shaped cookies while the oven preheats. WILD CHERRY SYRUP (Art of Drink, https://www.artofdrink.com/soda/cherry-phosphate): make it in one batch. The full recipe uses 1 oz bark, 1 fl oz glycerin, 4 fl oz water, a second 4 fl oz warm water, 4 fl oz cherry juice and 10 oz sugar, and makes 12 fl oz. Mix glycerin with the first 4 oz water, pour over the bark, macerate 24 h, then strain. Add the warm water to the bark for 1 h, strain, and combine. Add cherry juice, top up with water to 12 fl oz, and dissolve the sugar without heat. Each batch of cookies uses 2 Tbsp (1 fl oz) of syrup; 1/3 of the recipe covers 4 batches. FILLING per batch: simmer the preserves with 2 Tbsp syrup back to a thick jam, then cool. Off heat stir in 2/3 tsp acid phosphate, the drink ratio of 1 tsp per 1 1/2 oz syrup; add more to taste for extra tang. Fill about 1/2 tsp per cookie. Bake at 350\u00b0F for 12-13 min until edges just set. Dust with powdered sugar once cool. (Retro Soda Fountain 2026; base batch = 36.)"
  },
  {
   "recipe": "Coca-Cola Molasses Crinkle Cookies",
   "notes": "MOLASSES-STRENGTH COLA SYRUP: reduce Coca-Cola (Mexican, cane sugar) until it has about the same water content as molasses (~22%). Coke has 39 g sugar per 355 ml (~110 g per liter), so each liter reduces to about 141 g of syrup (~100 ml, a scant 1/2 cup). Method: weigh your empty pot, simmer flat Coke, and keep reducing until the contents weigh 141 g per liter you started with (2 L -> ~282 g). Near the end it will be bubbling around 225\u00b0F; trust the scale over the thermometer. Coke's phosphoric acid inverts some of the sugar as it cooks, which helps keep the syrup from crystallizing, like molasses. Swap it 1:1 by weight for molasses: 85 g (1/4 cup) per batch. Then whisk oil and sugars, add syrup, egg and vanilla, mix in dry, roll 1.5 in. balls in sugar, and bake at 350\u00b0F for 8-10 min. (Retro Soda Fountain 2026; base batch = 24.)"
  }
 ],
